  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-fall-2021-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(16{,}383 = 2^{14} - 1\\) \\(= (2^{7} - 1)(2^{7} + 1)\\) \\(= 127 \\cdot 129.\\) Then \\(129 = 3 \\cdot 43,\\) so \\(16{,}383 = 3 \\cdot 43 \\cdot 127.\\)\n\nThe greatest prime factor is \\(127,\\) whose digit sum is \\(1 + 2 + 7 = 10.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
